Mobile renderer: a project setting to turn ubershaders off

rendering/shader_compiler/ubershaders/enabled (default true). Off, a pipeline is compiled when first drawn.
Against godotengine/godot 4.7.2-stable (ed1daf0).

diff --git a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_mobile/render_forward_mobile.cpp b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_mobile/render_forward_mobile.cpp
index b30e19ca..aa312fca 100644
--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_mobile/render_forward_mobile.cpp
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_mobile/render_forward_mobile.cpp
@@ -3557,7 +3557,9 @@ void RenderForwardMobile::_update_shader_quality_settings() {
 RenderForwardMobile::RenderForwardMobile() {
 	singleton = this;
 
-	disable_ubershaders = RD::get_singleton()->get_driver_workarounds().disable_ubershaders;
+	// Without ubershaders, a pipeline is compiled when first drawn instead of ahead of time; some drivers keep
+	// a large amount of memory for every ubershader pipeline.
+	disable_ubershaders = RD::get_singleton()->get_driver_workarounds().disable_ubershaders || !bool(GLOBAL_DEF_RST("rendering/shader_compiler/ubershaders/enabled", true));
 	if (disable_ubershaders) {
 		print_verbose("Ubershaders: Disabled");
 	} else {
